-- =====================================================================
-- Round 49 -- item_template on-use / on-equip spells  (boot log 2026-09-01)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The whole "Loading Items..." error block from that boot resolves to one
-- root cause: Cataclysm item rows (VerifiedBuild 15050) were imported for the
-- map-750 Ashenvale/Azshara and map-861 Molten Front downports, and they carry
-- 4.3.4 field values the 3.3.5 client DBCs have no rows for.
--
--   1. 29 lines  "has wrong (not existing) spell in spellid_N"
--   2.  5 lines  "has bag family bit set not listed in ItemBagFamily.dbc"
--   3.  1 line   "Item (Entry: 49533) has wrong Map (256)"
--
-- (1) is NOT cosmetic.  Every one of the 22 items is a
-- `quest_template.StartItem` -- the source item handed to the player on quest
-- accept -- so the spell IS the quest mechanic.  ObjectMgr::LoadItemTemplates
-- zeroes an unresolvable SpellId, which leaves the item inert and the quest
-- uncompletable.  (2) and (3) really are cosmetic; the core strips the bad bag
-- bit itself, and a Map the client cannot resolve just never matches.
--
-- Screened before generating, same gate as round 40:
--   * all 23 logged ids exist in the Cata 4.3.4 Spell.dbc (73,281 rows);
--   * NONE exists in stock AC v19 Spell.dbc (49,839 rows) -- so this is a
--     never-downported gap, not a custom-DBC rebuild regression.
--
-- Generator: tools/gen_hyjal_spell_downport_r41.py  (read its header first)
-- Client side: the matching 28 rows are already appended to
-- `Custom/CSV DBC/Spell.csv`; Spell.dbc still has to be recompiled and packed
-- before tooltips/icons show.  The server resolves `spell_dbc` immediately.
-- =====================================================================


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. spell_dbc -- 28 spells (23 from the log + 5 EffectTriggerSpell closure)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The closure matters: 63566, 64075, 67914, 68411 and 69202 are the trigger
-- targets of five of the logged spells and are equally absent.  Shipping the
-- 23 alone would leave five dangling references -- the item resolves, the
-- spell it needs does not.
--
-- SUMMON / KILL_CREDIT2 EffectMiscValue creature entries were remapped to the
-- ids they actually live at here:
--     33736 -> 3633736   Fel Fire Bunny            (already imported)
--     35761 -> 3635761   Mortar Barrage            (imported in section 2)
--     35762 -> 3635762   Arcane Charge             (imported in section 2)
--     36130 -> 3636130   Scalding Water Lord       (imported in section 2)
--     33965                Felfire Projectile Bunny -- present at its STOCK
--                          WotLK id, deliberately NOT offset.
-- 3633736 is exactly what quest 13730 "Playing With Felfire" counts
-- (RequiredNpcOrGo1 = 3633736, count 7), so 63565 -> 63566 closes that quest
-- end to end.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (62817,62981,63565,64074,63797,65001,65115,65433,65739,67922,67923,68283,69635,68413,68422,68531,69217,69230,69743,69744,91647,97012,97324,63566,64075,67914,68411,69202);

